bench/step44/review-fixes/control_probe.mo:266:9: MO0304 this if is nested 4 deep in selected; the limit is 3, so move the inner block into its own function.
          if mode == "blocked-writer"
          ^
  why: Nesting is at most 3 deep (chapter 2, shape laws): each if, case, for, and block anonymous function is a level. The inner block becomes its own function.
bench/step44/review-fixes/control_probe.mo:246:13: MO0407 selected takes a Platform, which only main holds; take the parts it uses instead, such as an Fs or an Out.
  fn selected(platform: Platform, runtime: Runtime, mode: String) : UInt8
              ^
  why: A Platform exists only as fn main's parameter (Q18): main reads its parts and passes each one down, narrowed, so no other function can reach everything the program holds.
